    "result_text": "All 270 tests pass, including the new `Cp09Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners. Each new owner gets a `membershipNumber` equal to one more than the current owner count, persisted and returned as an integer in the owner response.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` (`integer`/`int32`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it's documented in the API contract.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membership_number` column with getter/setter (persistence is required because the acceptance test reads the value back via a separate `GET /api/owners/{id}` request).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Set `membershipNumber = findAllOwners().size() + 1` right before saving, after the duplicate checks.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the field automatically by name, so no mapper change was needed. The `Cp09Tests` invariant (two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) holds because each save increments the count seen by the next creation.",
